 "method": "STFT (1024-pt Hann, 128 hop) dominant-peak pitch track in 1.5-9.5 kHz; note segmentation on the 1.8-9 kHz band Hilbert envelope (3 ms smoothing): body pass onset -24 dB / offset -31 dB rel. file peak, min off-time 12 ms, min note 20 ms. Note f_start/f_end = median track over first/last 20% of the note; f_peak/f_min = 95th/5th percentile. peak_amp_rel = max of the 1.8-9 kHz band envelope (linear, signal peak-normalized) within the note. Contour and amplitude templates = per-note tracks resampled to 16 normalized points, median across instances of the type. Songs = note groups split at gaps > 1.0 s that contain an intro pair and a buzz. Type rules (this bird, by pitch/duration): I = flat 2300-2600 Hz, dur >= 0.15 s; B = flat 3700-4000 Hz, dur >= 0.40 s (the buzz); T = f_start >= 7500 Hz, dur >= 0.10 s (terminal high); H = f_peak >= 7000 Hz, dur >= 0.09 s (long high downslur \u2014 plausibly a fused h+M pair whose internal gap fell under the 12 ms segmentation floor); h = f_start >= 6000 Hz, dur < 0.09 s; M = f_start 4300-4800 Hz, dur <= 0.07 s; L = f_start 2000-2200 Hz rising to >= 2900 Hz; C = f_start 3300-3800 Hz falling to <= 3100 Hz, dur <= 0.07 s; W = flat 3400-3800 Hz chip (|f_end - f_start| < 400 Hz, f_peak < 3800 Hz). Two position rules: P = the short rising ticks (dur <= 0.05 s, f_peak >= 6000 Hz) that precede the first intro note of song 1; E = the flat ~4450 Hz short note immediately following a T. Contamination scan: short-time RMS in 0.25 s windows for the 60-500 Hz band and full band; a swell = 1 s-smoothed level > file median + 7 dB sustained >= 1.5 s (spans < 2 s apart merged). Gap contrast: 0.25 s full-band RMS windows, p10 (gap floor) vs p90 (phrase).",
